The first ones (up through C343-24) were posted in the thread wherein
the initial release of NH4 was announced.  But I'm creating a new
thread for this now...

C343-25 - Wear gauntlets of fumbling and walk around where there are
          such corpses.  "You see here a cockatrice corpse.  You trip
          over it.  You make a lot of noise!"  I have an NH4 save.
C343-26 - Go to Jubilex' Swamp and start zapping around with a wand
          of cold.  "The moat is bridged with ice!  You hear a
          cracking sound."  I have an NH4 save.
C343-27 - How should they slide?  You can only kick objects if you
          are not levitating.  On the plane of air, objects that are
          too heavy (e.g., dragon corpse) go "Thump" and send you
          backward a space, which seems logical to me.  Lighter
          items (e.g., a scroll) slide to the edge of the level.
          If there's a clear bug here, I haven't found it yet.
C343-28 - Status unknown; description is not very clear.
C343-29 - Confirmed.  This happens when you get the confirmation
          asking if you want to continue, so to reproduce it you
          have to be sufficiently encumbered to get that prompt
          (but not so encumbered as to be unable to apply a bag).
          It has to be a non-cursed BOH, because otherwise taking
          an item out of a container won't increase your level
          of encumbrance and you don't get the confirmation.
C343-30 - Fixed in NetHack 4 (credited to Alex Smith)
C343-31 - Reproduced in NH4 by wielding a boomerang in melee
          combat with negative luck.  It's debatable whether this
          is a bug; it seems generally in character with the way
          cockatrices and their corpses tend to stone you first and
          ask questions later, given anything resembling an excuse.
C343-32 - Use the "go down" command.  If you happen to be over the
          down stairs, it will tell you (presumably in order to
          explain why you can't go down) that you are floating
          high above the stairs.  Also, by searching, I was able
          to find bear traps and squeaky boards; probably other
          traps as well.  (Arguably, it *should* be possible to
          find falling rock traps, but not most of the others.)

